\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Five-Model Benchmark Performance Comparison: Highlighting trade-offs across binary IoU, multi-class mIoU, macro F1-score, pixel accuracy, and inference frame rate (FPS).}}{38}{figure.6.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Training Loss Convergence and Metric Trajectory: Demonstrating smooth monotonic reduction in compound Lov\'{a}sz-Softmax loss from 0.5995 down to 0.2102.}}{39}{figure.6.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Per-Class F1-Score and IoU Distribution: Demonstrating exceptional performance on key structural classes (Grass 0.85, Dry Roads 0.75, Dry Buildings 0.74, Trees 0.72, Water 0.64).}}{40}{figure.6.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces Qualitative Evaluation on Aerial Scene 10169: (Left to Right) Original UAV orthophoto, Ground Truth ColorMask, Standard $512 \times 512$ prediction, and Proposed SOTA High-Resolution Sliding-Window prediction. Note the sharp delineation of the swimming pool (yellow), parked vehicle (magenta), dry driveway (grey), and waterlogged field (cyan/green).}}{42}{figure.6.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces Qualitative Evaluation on Dense Residential Scene 10173: (Left to Right) Original UAV orthophoto, Ground Truth ColorMask, Standard $512 \times 512$ prediction, and Proposed SOTA High-Resolution Sliding-Window prediction. Notice how small vehicles in driveways and narrow street margins are crisply resolved rather than disappearing into blurred pixels.}}{42}{figure.6.5}%
